			"Message": "feat(Sky): Relay terminal shell execution lifecycle via OSC 633 sequences\n\nExtend the Sky bridge terminal data pipeline to parse VS Code shell integration OSC 633 sequences beyond the existing cwd (;P) handler. Add `OscEndPattern` (;D[;<exitCode>]) and `OscCmdLinePattern` (;E;<commandLine>) regex parsers, plus a per-terminal `InflightExecution` Map that stashes the most recent commandLine and cwd for each terminal id.\n\nOn receiving OSC 633 ; C (output begins), fire `localPty:shellExecutionStart` via Mountain IPC with the captured commandLine and cwd. On OSC 633 ; D (command finished), fire `localPty:shellExecutionEnd` with exitCode, commandLine, and cwd. The in-flight snapshot is cleared of commandLine after the end event so the next execution re-populates fresh.\n\nCocoon extensions can now subscribe to `vscode.window.onDidStartTerminalShellExecution` and `onDidEndTerminalShellExecution` with accurate command context.",
			"SHA": "8bf6245d60c90d63768563560deb8f774818acb3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T22:08:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Bridge editor lifecycle events to Mountain IPC\n\nForward four additional Monaco/workbench event streams through the Sky bridge layer so Cocoon extensions receive the corresponding VS Code API events:\n\n- `onDidScrollChange` fires at most ~16 fps (60 ms debounce) and emits `sky:editor:visibleRangesChanged` with the current visible ranges per editor — consumed by code lens providers, peek view, and minimap subscribers.\n- `onDidChangeConfiguration` emits `sky:editor:optionsChanged` carrying tabSize and insertSpaces so `vscode.window.onDidChangeTextEditorOptions` fires when the user toggles editor settings.\n- `onDidVisibleEditorsChange` (IEditorService) emits `sky:editor:visibleChanged` with the URI list of visible editors, preventing stale diagnostics from accumulating against closed tabs.\n- `onDidChangeActiveGroup`, `onDidAddGroup`, `onDidRemoveGroup`, and per-group `onDidModelChange` (IEditorGroupsService) emit `sky:editor:tabsChanged` with a full group/tab snapshot, enabling tab-level subscribers to react to open/close/move/pin.\n\nAll IPC calls are wrapped in try/catch and `.catch(() => {})` so the render pipeline is never interrupted by a failing Mountain call.",
			"SHA": "aecea637cdce3eb2f2a2d597b1530a3d1fa1c8b9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T19:29:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Replace bare specifier with relative path in workbench layouts\n\nThe three workbench layout entry points (Bundled Electron, standalone Electron, and Mountain Tauri) each imported the Sky bridge via the `@codeeditorland/sky` package specifier. When the build pipeline does not alias `@codeeditorland/sky` to the Sky source directory, this bare specifier can cause module resolution failures or produce duplicate copies of the bridge module in the bundle.\n\nReplace all three imports with explicit relative paths that resolve directly to `Function/Sky/Bridge.js` within the Sky source tree, ensuring deterministic module resolution across every workbench bootstrap path.",
			"SHA": "a55b46df905fa8d512b45cb05d6cc3caf30ce51a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T19:08:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				6
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Bridge extension IPC flows to workbench service layer\n\nRegister decoration types directly with ICodeEditorService in InstallTasksAndDecorations so that setDecorationsByType paints extension decorations (ESLint squiggles, GitLens blame, Error Lens) instead of silently dropping them. The previous DOM-event-only relay left Monaco's renderer with no registered styling.\n\nSwitch from the deprecated setDecorations to setDecorationsByType in InstallEditorOperations, matching the \"ext\" description used during type registration.\n\nWire panel-mode webview lifecycle in InstallWebview by subscribing to onMessage, onWillDispose, and onDidActiveEditorChange and forwarding them back to Cocoon via cocoon:notify, so extensions receive postMessage, dispose, and viewState events. Set disableServiceWorker: true (WKWebView refuses SW registration on vscode-webview://), add stable origin per viewType for session storage, and replay pending HTML from the race window before openWebview resolves. Resolve postMessage by handle (panel) in addition to viewId (sidebar).\n\nAdd sky://output/replace handler in InstallEditorAndOutput for atomic output channel buffer replacement matching upstream's replace() semantics, and honour preserveFocus on sky://output/show.\n\nRelay sky://tree-view/refresh from Cocoon to the workbench's ITreeView.refresh() in Bridge.ts, triggering fresh getChildren round-trips back to extensions.\n\nTogether these changes close the gap between Sky's bridge layer and the workbench service layer — decorations now paint, webview panels are interactive, output channels update atomically, and tree views respond to data changes.",
			"SHA": "52c452ced426f97e3693796a3488eca42c56d028"
		},
